# HQL core

HQL is a typed functional language for querying and manipulating HyperMarkDown
knowledge. The language is still being designed. This card describes the intended
core; the working bootstrap supports only Int, Float, Bool and same-type
numeric addition.

The core should stay small: typed values, bindings, ordinary functions, function
application and composition through `|`. Document and semantic types provide the
domain vocabulary. Most operations should be functions, with external capabilities
supplied by [[hql/extensions]]. HQL should develop its own functional syntax,
without adopting SQL clauses or Rust-like trait machinery.

## Value vocabulary

| Family | Types | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Documents | `Card`, `Frontmatter`, `Section`, `Link` | Authored knowledge and its structure |
| Semantic | `Concept`, `Relation`, `Proposition`, `Evidence` | Meaning, claims and support |
| Collections | `Set<T>`, `Seq<T>`, `Map<K,V>` | Membership, order and keyed lookup |
| Ordinary | `String`, `Int`, `Float`, `Bool`, `Date` | General computation |

These are the current design names. Generic types use angle brackets in these
pages; older corpus examples preserve other candidate spellings. Precise schemas,
declarations, polymorphism, optional/error types and Date operations remain open.
This vocabulary does not require each type to be a primitive in the evaluator.

## Bindings and values

```hql
alice : Card = resolve([[alice]])
```

`[[alice]]` is a reference literal. `resolve` is an ordinary function that resolves
it in the current context. The binding names the resulting Card; a filename does
not implicitly introduce a variable. Inferred binding is also preferred:

```hql
alice = resolve([[alice]])
```

An expression returns a typed value. A program returns its last expression;
earlier unbound values are discarded. Bindings retain values for later use.
Rendering belongs to the host, and printing or saving requires an explicit
effect. Constructing an updated Card does not itself persist a document.
The spelling of a no-result type, Unit or Void, remains open.

## Context values

`cards : Set<Card>` denotes the cards in the current vault or namespace. It
does not imply a traversal order. See [[hql/collections]].

`knowledge` denotes the semantic knowledge universe composed of concepts,
relations, propositions and evidence. It is richer than a collection of cards
or a graph. See [[hql/knowledge]].

```hql
knowledge
| graph
```

Pipes are fundamental to composition and querying. [[pipes]] describes the
execution direction; [[hql/knowledge]] records the unresolved distinction between
graph projection and presentation.

## Design boundaries

The host supplies a typed document model through an adapter to the existing HMD
parser and resolver. Raw HMD string searching is not the language's foundation.
Namespace imports belong in [[hql/extensions]], including optional `init.hql`.

The design baseline and unresolved choices are collected in [[hql/design-status]].
See also [[hql]], [[hmd-integration]] and the
[program-value model](../../models/behavior/program-values.md).
